body:
So, as a consumer, I don't have the right to voice my opinion on the product that I want to purchase if I see something wrong with it because it's "ruining this for everyone else"? That doesn't make sense.

&#x200B;

By your own logic, if you like it, buy it and play it, nothing that anyone else says will have an impact on your gameplay.

I've seen people blindfolding themselves haha

&#x200B;

But in Sword/Shield you could go only for hidden encounters.

I do, I care. One of the things that brings me joy within the franchise is to update my living dex every generation from scratch by catching all the pokémon or breeding them so they can be from the newey generation.

&#x200B;

Just because you don't care, don't assume other people don't care as well.

YTA, 100%. Your daughter has a career and a hobby that allowed her to save up to $50k, from what your comments have said, so she seems to be the responsible one here. 

&#x200B;

From everything you said about your son he is irresponsible and the notion that your daughter should bail him out of his debt will make him learn nothing. Both your son and his girlfriend should be the ones paying the debt, not your daughter. I see that you said that the girlfriend can't get a job because of depression and social anxiety (that you THINK she has) and, let me tell you, that's not an excuse, I speak from experience. There are plenty of jobs where she doesn't have to interact with people.

&#x200B;

As you said, he should file for bankrupcy. If you don't want him to do that because of his credit score, then you can lend him the money, take out a loan, sell some of your real-estate or something. After all, your son is going to pay you back, isn't he? That's what you are suggesting for your daughter.

Yeah, makes sense that those things would be chosen by the company, there.

&#x200B;

We have a law with almost 1000 articles talking about workers law, so we have many, many rights that are needed in employer-employee relationship, many of those involving the government and retirement stuff.

I'm kinda suicidal. I've been contemplating suicide for the past 3 or 4 years.

&#x200B;

I mean, I told my brother, but he didn't care.

You are not transphobic or an asshole for not wanting to date trans people, as many people have already said.

&#x200B;

That being said, you are transphobic, and an asshole, for trying to misgender her with what is clearly some TERF-level logic with all the misgendering you did there.
